1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,414
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,502
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,552 --> 00:00:18,413
Puss in Boots and the Ogre's Castle!

7
00:00:22,993 --> 00:00:27,193
Once upon a time, there was an
old miller who had three sons,

8
00:00:27,243 --> 00:00:31,657
a windmill, a grey donkey
and an orange striped cat.

9
00:00:32,287 --> 00:00:36,937
When the miller grew very old,
he divided everything he owned:

10
00:00:37,053 --> 00:00:40,698
the eldest son got the windmill,
the middle son got the donkey,

11
00:00:40,748 --> 00:00:44,370
and the youngest, whose name
was Tom, got only the cat.

12
00:00:44,510 --> 00:00:50,507
Tom sat down on a rock near the stream
and sighed, feeling very discouraged.

13
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:54,883
My brothers can grind wheat and carry
sacks, but what am I going to do with a

14
00:00:54,933 --> 00:00:55,621
cat?

15
00:00:55,671 --> 00:00:58,168
Tom said, scratching his head.

16
00:00:58,816 --> 00:01:02,674
The cat stretched, looked
Tom right in the eyes and,

17
00:01:02,732 --> 00:01:05,896
to everyone's surprise, began to talk.

18
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:09,937
Don't be sad, my friend.

19
00:01:10,102 --> 00:01:13,721
Find me a pair of boots and a cloth bag,
and you will see that I'm worth much

20
00:01:13,771 --> 00:01:14,974
more than a windmill,

21
00:01:15,024 --> 00:01:17,757
the cat said, swishing his tail.

22
00:01:18,329 --> 00:01:19,706
Hoo, hoo!

23
00:01:19,821 --> 00:01:22,865
A cat who talks and wants to wear boots?

24
00:01:22,984 --> 00:01:25,299
This story sounds promising,

25
00:01:25,349 --> 00:01:29,083
Popcorn said, from the
roof of the windmill.

26
00:01:30,137 --> 00:01:34,115
Tom spent his very last coins
on a pair of tall brown boots,

27
00:01:34,165 --> 00:01:37,843
and the cat pulled them
on, feeling very proud.

28
00:01:40,781 --> 00:01:44,967
He went into the forest, filled his
bag with fresh mushrooms and wild

29
00:01:45,017 --> 00:01:49,153
strawberries, and carried
everything to the king's castle.

30
00:01:52,628 --> 00:01:57,343
Your Majesty, my master, the Marquis
of Carabas, has sent you this gift,

31
00:01:57,393 --> 00:02:00,237
the cat said, with an elegant bow.

32
00:02:00,888 --> 00:02:06,005
The king had never heard of this marquis,
but he liked the strawberries very

33
00:02:06,055 --> 00:02:07,255
much.

34
00:02:07,662 --> 00:02:12,473
And so, every day for a whole month,
the cat brought the king gifts from the

35
00:02:12,523 --> 00:02:16,923
forest, always in the name
of the Marquis of Carabas.

36
00:02:18,033 --> 00:02:22,163
One day, the cat found out that the
king was going for a ride with his

37
00:02:22,213 --> 00:02:26,710
daughter, the princess, along
the road beside the river.

38
00:02:27,325 --> 00:02:31,357
Tom, go and take a bath in the river
right now, and leave the rest to me,

39
00:02:31,407 --> 00:02:33,432
the cat said, with a wink.

40
00:02:34,079 --> 00:02:38,737
Tom stepped into the river, but the
current was so strong that it carried away

41
00:02:38,787 --> 00:02:42,590
his old patched clothes,
which were lying on the bank.

42
00:02:44,765 --> 00:02:48,901
Just at that moment, the king's
carriage appeared on the road.

43
00:02:53,901 --> 00:02:56,732
Help, please, somebody come and help!

44
00:02:56,892 --> 00:03:00,601
The river has carried away all the
clothes of the Marquis of Carabas!

45
00:03:00,651 --> 00:03:03,787
the cat shouted, waving both paws.

46
00:03:04,416 --> 00:03:09,061
The king stopped the carriage, and asked
his servants to bring Tom the finest

47
00:03:09,111 --> 00:03:11,289
clothes from the royal trunk.

48
00:03:11,919 --> 00:03:16,994
When Tom came out of the river, all
dressed up, the princess looked at him and

49
00:03:17,044 --> 00:03:20,374
smiled, and he blushed bright red.

50
00:03:21,471 --> 00:03:24,573
The king invited Tom to ride
with them in the carriage,

51
00:03:24,623 --> 00:03:27,829
and the cat ran on ahead along the road.

52
00:03:28,439 --> 00:03:33,319
On the way, the cat met some farmers
working in an enormous wheat field,

53
00:03:33,369 --> 00:03:35,825
and they all looked very tired.

54
00:03:36,419 --> 00:03:38,217
Who do these lands belong to?

55
00:03:38,267 --> 00:03:40,306
the cat asked politely.

56
00:03:40,893 --> 00:03:44,333
They belong to a bossy ogre
who lives in that grey castle,

57
00:03:44,383 --> 00:03:46,657
and he takes almost all of our harvest,

58
00:03:46,707 --> 00:03:50,066
one farmer answered, with a sad face.

59
00:03:50,733 --> 00:03:53,508
The cat thought for a moment and said:

60
00:03:53,605 --> 00:03:57,467
Then help me: when the king passes by,
tell him these fields belong to the

61
00:03:57,517 --> 00:04:01,957
Marquis of Carabas, and I promise you
will never have to obey the ogre again.

62
00:04:02,575 --> 00:04:07,253
The farmers looked at one another,
smiled, and agreed to the plan.

63
00:04:07,876 --> 00:04:12,826
When the carriage passed by, the king
asked who owned those beautiful fields,

64
00:04:12,876 --> 00:04:17,693
and everyone answered together that
they belonged to the Marquis of Carabas.

65
00:04:18,805 --> 00:04:24,274
Meanwhile, the cat reached the grey
castle and knocked on the enormous door.

66
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,529
The ogre opened the door,
looked down, and grumbled:

67
00:04:29,579 --> 00:04:32,717
Who are you, and what do
you want in my castle?

68
00:04:33,290 --> 00:04:37,187
Mister Ogre, people say that you can
turn yourself into any animal at all,

69
00:04:37,237 --> 00:04:39,299
but I find that very hard to believe,

70
00:04:39,349 --> 00:04:41,416
the cat said, with a bow.

71
00:04:42,101 --> 00:04:46,571
The ogre felt very proud of
himself, gave a big laugh and,

72
00:04:46,712 --> 00:04:51,432
in a cloud of sparkling smoke,
turned into an enormous lion.

73
00:04:55,022 --> 00:04:59,139
The cat got such a fright that he
jumped up onto a tall bookshelf,

74
00:04:59,189 --> 00:05:01,436
with his tail all puffed up.

75
00:05:02,073 --> 00:05:04,406
Very impressive, Mister Ogre!

76
00:05:04,533 --> 00:05:08,199
But I bet you can't turn into a
very small animal, like a mouse,

77
00:05:08,249 --> 00:05:11,344
the cat said, from the
top of the bookshelf.

78
00:05:12,339 --> 00:05:14,622
That is far too easy for me!

79
00:05:14,672 --> 00:05:19,664
the ogre said, and in another cloud
of smoke, he turned into a small grey

80
00:05:19,714 --> 00:05:21,697
mouse with big ears.

81
00:05:25,292 --> 00:05:28,769
The cat climbed down from
the bookshelf very slowly,

82
00:05:28,819 --> 00:05:31,664
but he did not pounce on the mouse.

83
00:05:32,278 --> 00:05:34,415
Now listen carefully, Mister Ogre:

84
00:05:34,465 --> 00:05:38,466
leave this castle, leave the farmers in
peace, and never be bossy with anyone

85
00:05:38,516 --> 00:05:39,513
ever again,

86
00:05:39,563 --> 00:05:42,019
the cat said, in a firm voice.

87
00:05:42,656 --> 00:05:46,314
The mouse was so embarrassed that he
didn't even try to turn back into an

88
00:05:46,364 --> 00:05:52,139
ogre, and he ran off through a hole
in the wall, to live very far away.

89
00:05:54,998 --> 00:05:56,375
Hoo, hoo!

90
00:05:56,477 --> 00:05:58,180
What a clever cat!

91
00:05:58,265 --> 00:06:01,151
He beat the ogre without hurting anyone,

92
00:06:01,201 --> 00:06:05,240
Popcorn said, flapping her
wings on the chandelier.

93
00:06:06,311 --> 00:06:10,261
Soon after, the king's
carriage arrived at the castle,

94
00:06:10,311 --> 00:06:12,697
and the cat ran to open the door.

95
00:06:17,690 --> 00:06:21,506
Welcome, Your Majesty and dear princess,
to the castle of the Marquis of

96
00:06:21,556 --> 00:06:22,443
Carabas!

97
00:06:22,493 --> 00:06:26,685
the cat said, with the most
elegant bow of his whole life.

98
00:06:27,334 --> 00:06:31,798
The king was delighted with the castle,
and everyone sat down to a feast of

99
00:06:31,848 --> 00:06:35,220
warm bread, pumpkin soup and apple pie.

100
00:06:35,868 --> 00:06:39,999
But Tom felt uneasy, pushing
his food around his plate,

101
00:06:40,049 --> 00:06:43,657
because he knew that not
all of it was really true.

102
00:06:44,768 --> 00:06:48,954
At the end of the feast, Tom
stood up, took a deep breath,

103
00:06:49,004 --> 00:06:50,807
and spoke from his heart.

104
00:06:51,433 --> 00:06:54,146
Your Majesty, I have
to tell you the truth:

105
00:06:54,246 --> 00:06:57,583
I am not a marquis at all,
I am just a miller's son,

106
00:06:57,633 --> 00:06:59,398
and all I own is this cat,

107
00:06:59,448 --> 00:07:01,390
Tom said, looking down.

108
00:07:02,058 --> 00:07:06,431
The king was quiet for a moment,
and then he gave a kind smile.

109
00:07:07,013 --> 00:07:10,550
A young man who is brave enough to
tell the truth is worth more than any

110
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,054
marquis in the world,

111
00:07:12,104 --> 00:07:15,963
the king said, putting his
hand on Tom's shoulder.

112
00:07:16,605 --> 00:07:21,527
The princess smiled too, and said that
she liked Tom for his gentle heart,

113
00:07:21,577 --> 00:07:23,741
and not for any title.

114
00:07:24,366 --> 00:07:28,344
Tom shared the land with the farmers,
and from then on they all worked

115
00:07:28,394 --> 00:07:31,336
together and divided the harvest fairly.

116
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:33,254
And the cat?

117
00:07:33,492 --> 00:07:38,345
He took off his boots, lay down by the
fire, and never had to chase anything

118
00:07:38,395 --> 00:07:41,433
ever again, except balls of wool.

119
00:07:41,517 --> 00:07:42,894
Hoo, hoo!

120
00:07:43,001 --> 00:07:48,027
Cleverness helps a lot, but friendship
and the truth are worth even more,

121
00:07:48,077 --> 00:07:51,449
Popcorn said, blinking her big eyes.

122
00:07:58,754 --> 00:07:59,954
The End.

123
00:08:01,669 --> 00:08:02,381
Hoo...

124
00:08:02,431 --> 00:08:03,455
Psst!

125
00:08:03,505 --> 00:08:05,077
Are you still awake?

126
00:08:05,230 --> 00:08:07,283
Did you like tonight's story?

127
00:08:07,405 --> 00:08:10,845
Puss in Boots showed us
that cleverness helps a lot,

128
00:08:10,895 --> 00:08:14,446
but that friendship and the
truth are worth even more.

129
00:08:14,718 --> 00:08:19,025
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

130
00:08:19,321 --> 00:08:24,219
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

131
00:08:24,269 --> 00:08:26,674
for more stories at bedtime.

132
00:08:26,978 --> 00:08:28,178
Hoo...

